WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:25.730
He isn’t a well-known leader and he doesn’t
run a state, so much as a relatively small

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.730
country.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.509
And officially he isn’t even that country’s
top leader.

00:00:29.509 --> 00:00:35.790
Despite all this, on June 2nd 2019, the New
York Times published a report declaring Mohammed

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.200
bin Zayed as the world's most powerful political
leader in the Arab world.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.360
He even ranks above the new de facto Saudi
Arabian leader, Mohammed bin Salman, of whom

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.250
we’ve already spoken here on VISUALPOLITIK.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.220
I’ll leave some links to videos in the description.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.210
After the New York Times report was published,
we asked ourselves a few questions:

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.260
Who exactly is Mohammed bin Zayed?

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.540
What are the keys to his power?

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.540
Is he really the most powerful Arab political
leader in the world?

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.650
Listen up.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:10.530
(INTRO)

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.260
Mohammed bin Zayed is the crown prince of
Abu Dhabi, the richest and most powerful emirate

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:20.170
of the United Arab Emirates.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:27.621
He is also the deputy supreme commander of
the Emirates’ armed forces and the President

00:01:27.621 --> 00:01:32.330
of the Abu Dhabi Executive Council, that is,
the President of the Abu Dhabi government.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:36.700
Quite a feat.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.030
And it’s his political abilities along with
the poor health of his older brother, Sheikh

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.070
Khalifa bin Zayed, that have made him Abu
Dhabi’s de facto leader and by extension

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.000
the leader of all the United Arab Emirates.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.070
As many of you know, the United Arab Emirates
is a small country, located in the Persian

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.300
Gulf and similar in size to Panama or South
Carolina.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.479
We’re talking about a country made up of
seven different emirates out of which the

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.320
two best known by far are Abu Dhabi and Dubai.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.830
In fact, even though this country is made
up of seven emirates, the truth is that, at

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:16.340
the political level, Abu Dhabi is by far the
most important emirate, why?

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.090
We’ll see that later in this video, but
we can already give you quite a weighty reason:

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:25.870
Abu Dhabi holds more than 90% of all of the
Arab Emirates oil reserves.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:49.030
But for now, let's go back to Mohammed bin
Zayed.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:53.890
This character was born in 1961 and was the
third son of Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan, the

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.180
first president of the United Arab Emirates.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.290
From a young age he focused his career on
the army, where he became an air force pilot.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.940
And the armed forces is where he also started
his political career.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:12.560
In 1991, just after Saddam Hussein initiated
Iraq’s invasion of Kuwait, the then Emirati

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.730
air forces commander landed in Washington
with a mission:

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.640
To buy all possible military equipment.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.000
Hellfire missiles, Apache helicopters, F16
planes.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.530
They wanted the full package.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.680
From that moment on, Mohammed bin Zayed became
one of Washington's closest allies, not only

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.209
within the Arab countries but on the entire
planet.

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:38.980
Because we’re talking about a political
leader who over the years has become one of

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:44.760
the icons of reform and openness in the Arab
world.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.170
Under his management, Abu Dhabi has taken
pioneering steps, both in Dubai’s economic

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.180
and civil matters.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.370
And on some issues, they went even further.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:58.319
Perhaps the best proof of this is the Pope’s
own visit to the Emirates, which we recently

00:03:58.319 --> 00:03:59.730
covered here on VISUALPOLITIK.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:04.290
However, even though he was leading a reform
program that has made the Emirates perhaps

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:09.709
the most open and prosperous country in the
Arab world, Mohammed bin Zayed also fiercely

00:04:09.709 --> 00:04:15.330
supports an idea that can sound, at the very
least, controversial: That the Arab world

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.889
isn’t ready for democracy right now.

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:19.789
Yes, you heard that correctly.

00:04:19.789 --> 00:04:24.080
According to bin Zayed, openness in the Arab
world can only come about to those nations

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.330
led by authoritarian regimes.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.080
Promoting democracy would only feed fundamentalist
groups that would end up winning the elections.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.060
It’s an idea that is actively defended and
has significantly shaped the Emirates’ external

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.789
relations in recent years.

00:04:37.789 --> 00:04:43.669
But, having said this, I think we now have
to turn to the key question of this video:

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:48.120
Where does this character fit in and how much
power does he really have?

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:54.659
Let's examine the three main areas that form
the foundations of his power.

00:04:54.659 --> 00:05:00.379
Listen up.

00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:03.240
(1.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.909
THE POWER OF THE PORTFOLIO)

00:05:05.909 --> 00:05:10.949
I don't think anyone will find it strange
if I say that money has always been one of

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:13.439
the most important elements in power.

00:05:13.439 --> 00:05:17.619
Well, if Arab countries have been famous for
anything, it has been for their conspicuous

00:05:17.619 --> 00:05:18.619
consumption.

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:22.729
They are no strangers to spending indecent
amounts of money on all kinds of things, whims

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:24.979
or projects that led nowhere, right?

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:28.800
Well, in this case, besides spending a lot
of money on all kinds of public projects,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.150
what the Emirates have also done has been
to save and invest a good part of their money

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.240
all over the planet.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:43.280
To the point that today, Mohammed bin Zayed
has one of the fullest portfolios we can imagine

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.280
at his disposal.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.750
But the question is, exactly how much money
do the Emirates and Abu Dhabi have saved in

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.160
their sovereign wealth funds?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.930
How much are we really talking about?

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.090
For those who don’t know, a sovereign fund
is an investment fund that a government creates

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.710
to invest its savings in assets to generate
profitability.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:03.259
Basically, it’s like any saver’s investment
fund.

00:06:03.259 --> 00:06:08.650
Well, according to the latest estimates, the
United Arab Emirates’ sovereign funds have

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:14.330
accumulated investments worth more than 1.3
trillion dollars.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:19.059
Out of this amount, just over 900 billion
dollars are concentrated in Abu Dhabi’s

00:06:19.059 --> 00:06:22.559
two main sovereign wealth funds:

00:06:22.559 --> 00:06:27.720
Abu Dhabi’s investment authority controls
almost 700 billion, making it the third largest

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.300
sovereign fund in the world

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.300
(CHART)

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.930
And Mubadala’s fund has just over 220 billion
US dollars.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:38.139
We’re talking about a huge fortune.

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:43.599
More than 900 billion saved by the Emirate
of Abu Dhabi and invested throughout the world

00:06:43.599 --> 00:06:49.259
in stocks, debts, buildings, highways, ports,
airports, banks, hospitals, hotels, factories,

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:52.939
mines, even ice cream parlors... everything.

00:06:52.939 --> 00:06:56.569
And that explains why you see news stories
like these:

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:03.759
(AUDIO: Abu Dhabi pays Abertis 495 million
for 20% of its Chilean subsidiary.

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:04.759
El País)

00:07:04.759 --> 00:07:09.220
(AUDIO: Abu Dhabi Investment Authority to
invest $50 billion into India.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:13.090
One of the largest sovereign funds in the
world, the Abu Dhabi Investment Authority

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:23.370
will $50 billion into India, especially into
infrastructure and food processing capacity.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:24.370
The Times of India)

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.999
But let’s be careful here, because power
doesn’t only consist of having a full portfolio

00:07:26.999 --> 00:07:32.139
but also of controlling assets and companies
of all kinds throughout the entire planet

00:07:32.139 --> 00:07:36.060
and to have a cashflow that is very, very
coveted by most governments.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:39.110
Who doesn’t want a few billion invested
in their country?

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:46.009
That’s pure diplomacy.

00:07:46.009 --> 00:07:48.419
In any case there’s a detail we cannot skip.

00:07:48.419 --> 00:07:53.069
You see, the Emirate of Abu Dhabi only has
a population of 2.7 million people, out of

00:07:53.069 --> 00:07:56.580
which just over half a million have Emirati
nationality.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.319
That is, the Emirate of Abu Dhabi’s savings
alone in its two main sovereign funds amounts

00:08:01.319 --> 00:08:07.970
to more than 340 thousand dollars per inhabitant
and more than 1.6 million per citizen of Abu

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.490
Dhabi with Emirati nationality.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:10.490
1.6 million dollars.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.849
They’ve been saving since 1976.

00:08:12.849 --> 00:08:16.199
And even though they’re sitting on such
a large amount of money, they take the fact

00:08:16.199 --> 00:08:19.680
that the government doesn’t have a public
deficit very seriously.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.830
(AUDIO: Abu Dhabi to see a budget surplus
in 2019 thanks to public consolidation efforts.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:25.830
Oxford Business Group)

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:31.469
But that isn’t the only key to Mohammed
bin Zayed's power.

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:35.060
(2.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.040
THE POWER OF FORCE)

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.349
This is perhaps the Emirates’ least known
aspect, but in recent years this small country

00:08:43.349 --> 00:08:45.990
has earned itself the nickname “little Sparta”.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:50.690
The United Arab Emirates army is very small,
it has just over 60,000 soldiers.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:55.260
But in the last two decades, under Mohammed
bin Zayed’s command along with a lot of

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.350
experts among whom is the former US secretary
of defense, Jim Mattis, this army has been

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.580
restructured around one simple idea:

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:12.630
To be a small but very well equipped, agile
and well-trained army.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:16.880
To achieve this, the Emirates’ military
budget exceeds 20 billion dollars every year.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.010
This has allowed them to buy all kinds of
foreign equipment:

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:25.891
70 F-16 updated with the latest technology;
more 70 Mirage; 30 apaches, 19 chinook, more

00:09:25.891 --> 00:09:31.020
than 400 Leclerc tanks, 76 scorpions, thousands
of armored vehicles of all kinds, dozens of

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:35.800
drones, the patriot missile system... they
even bought the crown jewel, the THAAD missile

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:42.810
system, one of the most modern systems in
the United States.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.840
The same one that the US power deployed in
South Korea, causing a huge confrontation

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:51.750
with China.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.110
And this is just the beginning, for example
they are now looking at the F-35.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:59.430
In fact, after Saudi Arabia, Emirates is the
second largest buyer of technology and military

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.200
equipment from the United States.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.990
But, if the Arab armies have traditionally
been known for something, it has been for

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:09.680
spending a lot of money on equipment, and
when the time comes, not really taking advantage

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:10.680
of it.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:14.380
That’s why another of Mohammed bin Zayed’s
priorities has been to ensure that the Emirati

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.600
army is well trained.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:21.200
And how do you think they went about it?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:28.760
Well, in addition to paying for all kinds
of training courses abroad, the Emirati army

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.980
has committed itself to going into combat
in the last few years, especially hand in

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.930
hand with the United States itself.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:36.940
You heard that right.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.400
Since 2003, Emirates has deployed elite troops
in Afghanistan, sent troops to Somalia to

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:46.160
combat piracy and after the United States,
it has been the country that has carried out

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.840
the most air missions against the Islamic
State.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.720
Always hand in hand with the United States.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:55.220
And not only that, they have also recently
intervened, on their own, in Libya, in northern

00:10:55.220 --> 00:11:01.810
Sinai, in Egypt and massively in Yemen.

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:05.630
Of course, they’ve also hired lots of experts
from around the world, so much so that some

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.990
units are even under the command of foreign
officers.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.200
In other words, they have contracted their
own officers.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:16.370
This is the case, for example, of General
Toumajan (Tumeijan), a former lieutenant colonel

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:21.000
of the United States Army who is now in command
of the Emirati helicopter division; or Australian

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:25.650
Mike Hindmarsh, who runs the Presidential
Guard.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:29.700
The result is that today the Emirati army
is not only considered one of the best equipped

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.630
armies but also the best trained one throughout
the region.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.610
Come on, they’re catching up with Israel,
a country from which they’re currently buying

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:36.610
technology.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:37.610
And that's not all.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:40.810
in another move to gain autonomy, the Emirati
authorities have reinstated the mandatory

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:45.140
military service and have invested a lot of
money to develop a full national weapons industry.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.660
A military industry of its own.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.800
Of course, always hand-in-hand with large
multinationals and their technology.

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.920
And the truth is that it’s working.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:12:02.590
There are currently almost 200 Emirati defense
companies manufacturing all kinds of equipment:

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.630
Armored vehicles, guided missiles, drones,
light airplanes...

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.450
All manufactured in the Emirates.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:11.930
Now they are even trying to develop their
own propeller bomber to operate at low altitude

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.350
on counterinsurgency missions.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.870
But wait, there’s more.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:23.000
Emirates has opened military bases in places
like Yemen, Eritrea and Somaliland – which

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.730
is unprecedented – and has prepared to operate
alongside mercenary armies.

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:30.820
Elite mercenaries led by Erik Prince, the
founder and owner of the Blackwater company,

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:33.630
which complement the capabilities of their
own army.

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:37.250
(Emirates Secretly Sends Colombian Mercenaries
to Yemen Fight.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:38.250
NYT)

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.750
In short, this is the change that is taking
place in the Emirati army and which has earned

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.360
them the name “little Sparta”.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.710
All by the hand of our central character.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.500
But this isn't his only weapon

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:54.900
(3.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:58.740
GEOSTRATEGY IN FORCE)

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:03.600
With proven reserves of more than 97 billion
barrels, the Emirates has the seventh largest

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:09.420
conventional oil reserve on the planet under
its own subsoil.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:14.250
They are currently producing about 3 million
barrels per day and expect to reach four million

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.230
by 2020 and five million by 2030.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.960
That is a lot, a lot of oil.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:23.290
So with all that oil and all the money we’ve
seen, Mohammed bin Zayed has launched a diplomatic

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:27.510
career across the planet that has multiplied
this small country’s international influence

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:28.850
in recent years.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:34.040
India, Indonesia, Ethiopia... and of course
the United States.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.480
His relations with the Trump administration
are formidable.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:41.510
The truth is that with such assets under their
belts, no door remains closed.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:47.110
And, if we add to all this the fact that the
Emirates has become an important financial,

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:51.740
commercial, logistic and even tourist center
in the last two decades and that this man,

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:56.490
Mohammed bin Zayed, is practically leading
everything, it doesn’t seem crazy to state

00:13:56.490 --> 00:14:02.600
that, today, he is the most powerful Arab
political leader in the world.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.740
Of course, being the most powerful Arab doesn’t
mean it’s all smooth sailing.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.740
Not at all.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.820
Qatar’s blockade has been a resounding failure.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:17.430
But that is something we covered in a past
video.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:31.430
So I

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:45.240
really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

